{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MgF2cpazTkPrjiyqKMkhz5","type":"tool_result","content":"  {\"id\": \"contract-forward-hints\", \"concept\": \"The live contract leaks upcoming days: tokens and day numbers that do not belong to today\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D19 leaked D20's overlay magic ('PK19 for Day 19 or RS20 for Day 20') and it came true. Still open after D21 (D20/D21 contracts added no new token; carried-over questions byte-identical): the format enum lists `neko_bytecode` (unseen), and d07_analysis_method_count says 'for Day 26 use the primary classfile named by that unit'. Each day, grep the contract for magic-like tokens (`[A-Z]{2}\\\\d{2}`), enum values never confirmed, and 'Day NN' > today; record them in solver/NOTES.md and the coverage atlas so the prebuild targets them. The solver maps a `<2 caps><NN>` magic to the group whose day is NN. D22: no new token/day; all members silently renamed dNN--variant-000.* -> dNN--sample.* and the d03 questions dropped 'variant-' -- solvers must not key on 'variant-'. D23: no new token/day either (Day 26 and neko_bytecode still open). D24: no new token/day; EVERY question reworded into a spec (sha256 'ZIP central-directory order (1-based)', format rule list, full HCFG layout + per-container carrier rule) -- Day 26 + neko_bytecode still open; D24 Scala's `Foo$` module vs forwarder Main-Class is a plausible meaning of 'primary classfile named by that unit'. D25: no new token/day; d25 ids copy the D24 wording verbatim; Day 26 + neko_bytecode still open (Clojure's `__init` vs gen-class stub is a 2nd example of 'primary classfile named by that unit'). D26: the d07 'for Day 26 use the primary classfile named by that unit' leak came TRUE (Groovy jar; the primary classfile = the manifest Main-Class `Day26Variant000`, not the `$_main_closure1` closure). Only `neko_bytecode` remains open; D26 contract added no new token/day.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"diec\", \"concept\": \"Compiler/packer/language fingerprint for unknown toolchains\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release horsicq/DIE-engine (die_lin64_portable tar) -> `diec -j F`. Complements `rz-bin -I` lang= and the STEP 3 strings regex when a new language lands.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"checksec-fields\", \"concept\": \"PIE/RELRO/NX/canary/static as answer fields\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"`rz-bin -I` already prints pic/relro/nx/canary/static/stripped. GM spelling unknown: relro full/partial/none, booleans true/false like has_symtab. Add to playbook naming law before first sighting; no checksec install needed.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"new-language-fingerprints\", \"concept\": \"V, Odin, Modula-2, Kotlin/Native, Dart AOT, Nuitka, Erlang, Julia, Zig-cc/Nim-js... (Ada D17, Fortran D18, COBOL D19, Haskell D20, OCaml D21 seen)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Cue strings are in the Recognition cues STEP 3 regex. All still answer format=elf/architecture=x86-64 per the D8-D15 law; risk is only where the HCFG literal lives (compressed Dart snapshot, Nuitka constants blob, GHC closures) -> hcfg_scan then Ghidra. Ada/Fortran/COBOL/Haskell/OCaml all landed as plain x86-64 ELFs (format elf) -- the law held; D19-D20 moved the HCFG into an overlay, D21 into a separate plugin member. gfortran/gnat/ocaml/ghc are NOT installed for fixture builds (apt gfortran gnat ocaml-nox ghc if prebuilds are wanted).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"provenance-facts-extractor\", \"concept\": \"Build provenance fields: GNU build-id, .comment compiler banner, DWARF producer/language/comp_dir, PE TimeDateStamp/PDB path/Rich, Go/Rust toolchain version\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). Implement in the facts dict so a new id answers without code: build_id = lowercase hex of NT_GNU_BUILD_ID desc (no 0x), compiler = first `.comment` string, dwarf_producer via pyelftools, pdb_path from RSDS, timestamp as ...\"},\n  {\"id\": \"language-detector\", \"concept\": \"lib.binary.language_of(data) -> source language/toolchain token with evidence, for all 17 seen languages + next candidates\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). A `language`/`compiler`/`toolchain` id on any group would need consistent tokens: c, cpp, csharp/dotnet, go, rust, java, kotlin, swift, nim, zig, d, pascal/fpc, crystal, objc, wat/wasm, ada; candidates haskell, ocaml, ...\"},\n  {\"id\": \"build-pair-router\", \"concept\": \"Same-source build PAIRS beyond stripped/symbolized and compact/direct (static/dynamic, O0/O2/Os, pie/nopie, debug/release, packed/unpacked, plain/obfuscated)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). D15 and D16 were both 'one source, two builds' with `dNN_analysis_<tag>_<field>` ids. Fixtures: gcc -O0 vs -O2, -static vs dynamic, -pie vs -no-pie, -g vs stripped, upx'd vs plain, each with a `.hcfg` section and ... D24 SEEN as a vulnerable/corrected twin (Scala jars) -- the generic qualifier peel covered it with zero code.\"},\n| 14 | OCaml native | **seen D21** (4.02.3: loader PIE 780 KB with debug_info + Dynlink; plugin `.cmxs` ET_DYN 9 KB, HCFG RAW `.data` = `camlPlugin_000__1`) | `caml_startup`, `camlStdlib__`/`camlCamlinternalFormat__`, `caml_main`, `OCAMLRUNPARAM`, version string `4.02.3`; `.cmxs`: `caml_plugin_header`, `Caml2007D002` | [I] `nm f \\| grep -m5 '^.* T caml'`; `nm -D --defined-only f.cmxs`; `grep -abo HCFG f.cmxs`; [M] ocaml | high (carry-over; d21 theme facts = backfill candidates) |\n| 15 | V language | gap | `main__main`, `v__`/`builtin__` symbols, compiled via C (`.comment` GCC/tcc) | [I] `nm f \\| grep -E 'main__main\\|builtin__'` | low-med |\n| 26 | musl / static linking | seen D4, D5, D8, D12 (static); musl gap | no `.interp`, no `.dynamic`; musl: no `GLIBC_2.` version strings, `__libc_start_main` absent | [I] `readelf -lW f \\| grep -c INTERP`; `strings -a f \\| grep -c GLIBC_` | med (cheap twist \"Static\") |\n| 63 | Build provenance: GNU build-id, `.comment` compiler banner, Go buildinfo, rustc commit, PE timestamp/Rich/PDB | gap (Go buildinfo used internally) | `.note.gnu.build-id` (20-byte SHA1), `GCC: (Debian 15...)`, `go1.NN`, `/rustc/<sha>`, `TimeDateStamp`, RSDS | [I] `readelf -nW f`; `readelf -p .comment f`; `go version -m f`; `pefile` `FILE_HEADER.TimeDateStamp` | med (natural \"compiler/language\" id; label spelling unknown) |\n| 100 | DWARF deep facts (CU names/languages, DW_AT_producer, function names + line ranges, type names) | gap (D21 loader shipped `with debug_info`; prebuilt provenance covers producer) | `.debug_info`/`.debug_line` present, `file` says \"with debug_info\" | [I] `llvm-dwarfdump-18 --debug-info f`; pyelftools DWARF | med |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b17b27cc-347b-41e9-a1e7-6aa9a3b67bd6","uuid":"f7afb7de-a3a8-4433-9879-b893e8b63069","timestamp":"2026-10-27T13:09:05.281Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"  {\"id\": \"contract-forward-hints\", \"concept\": \"The live contract leaks upcoming days: tokens and day numbers that do not belong to today\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D19 leaked D20's overlay magic ('PK19 for Day 19 or RS20 for Day 20') and it came true. Still open after D21 (D20/D21 contracts added no new token; carried-over questions byte-identical): the format enum lists `neko_bytecode` (unseen), and d07_analysis_method_count says 'for Day 26 use the primary classfile named by that unit'. Each day, grep the contract for magic-like tokens (`[A-Z]{2}\\\\d{2}`), enum values never confirmed, and 'Day NN' > today; record them in solver/NOTES.md and the coverage atlas so the prebuild targets them. The solver maps a `<2 caps><NN>` magic to the group whose day is NN. D22: no new token/day; all members silently renamed dNN--variant-000.* -> dNN--sample.* and the d03 questions dropped 'variant-' -- solvers must not key on 'variant-'. D23: