"\nbyid['build-pair-router']['detail']+=\" D27 SEEN as a compiler-named twin (`-gcc.elf`/`-tcc.elf`, ids `gcc_format`/`tcc_machine`/`gcc_config_*`): the generic qualifier peel covered it with zero code.\"\nbyid['new-language-fingerprints']['detail']+=\" D27: V landed (transpiled to C, built by gcc AND tcc, musl-dynamic ELF, format elf / machine 62 per build) -- the law held again. Remaining transpile-to-C candidates: Vala/Genie, Cython, hxcpp, Chicken Scheme; own-backend: Odin, Hare.\"\nbyid['contract-forward-hints']['detail']+=\" D27: no new token/day; the HCFG rule for d27 was reworded to 'Scan backward from the end of the member for literal HCFG magic and accept the first CRC32-valid' (direction is part of the spec). Only `neko_bytecode` remains open.\"\nif 'theme-facts-recording' in byid:\n    byid['theme-facts-recording']['detail']+=\" D27 (attribution, unasked): record per build DW_AT_producer, debug format (DWARF version / STABS), linker layout cues (section merging, note count, .gnu.hash vs .hash), libc (PT_INTERP/NEEDED), symbol count and IPA suffixes, size.\"\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"compiler-attribution-facts\",\"concept\":\"Per-build compiler attribution facts for same-source twins (gcc vs tcc on D27; clang, zig cc, MSVC, MinGW, icx next): compiler name, version, flags, evidence list -- with banners stripped\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"D27 'Compiler Says What' asked nothing about it, but the prompt ('name the toolchain -- attribute this binary to its maker') makes per-build fields the obvious backfill/sequel: <role>_compiler, compiler_version, producer, toolchain. Build lib.binary.compiler_attribution(data) -> {compiler, version, flags, evidence[]} in priority order: DW_AT_producer (gcc `GNU C99 12.2.1 20220924 ... -Os`, clang `clang version N`), `.comment` (often ABSENT: D27 had none), gcc IPA/LTO suffixes `.lto_priv.N/.constprop.N/.isra.N/.part.N/.cold`, FILE `crtstuff.c`; tcc = `.stab`/`.stabstr`, `tcc_backtrace`/`tcc_state` syms, `.hash` without `.gnu.hash`, unmerged input sections (`.text._start_c`, `.rodata.str1.1`, `.data.ro`, `.data.rel.ro.local`), one NT_GNU_PROPERTY note per input object, FILE `<command line>`; clang = `.llvm_addrsig`, `__llvm_*`; zig cc = `zig` in .comment/compiler-rt syms. Fixtures: build one C file with gcc, clang-18, tcc (apt tcc) and zig cc if available, each with/without -g and stripped .comment (`objcopy -R .comment`); test that the token survives stripping. Lowercase tool tokens (gcc/tcc/clang/msvc/mingw) as the presumed spelling.\"},\n {\"id\":\"linker-fingerprint-facts\",\"concept\":\"Linker attribution from layout: GNU ld.bfd vs gold vs lld vs mold vs tcc's built-in linker vs MSVC link.exe / GNU ld for PE\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"D27 prompt: 'Compare the runtime and linker fingerprints across builds'. Cues: gold `.note.gnu.gold-version`; lld `.comment` 'Linker: LLD N', typical 4 PT_LOAD with separate R/RX/RW, `.rela.dyn` before `.rela.plt` ordering; mold `.comment` 'mold N'; ld.bfd merges `.text.*` into `.text` and emits one combined .note.gnu.property, `.gnu.hash` + `.hash` per --hash-style; tcc keeps input section names and one GNU_PROPERTY note per object, `.hash` only, no `.eh_frame_hdr`, no `.gnu.version*`; PE: OptionalHeader Major/MinorLinkerVersion (MSVC 14.x, GNU ld 2.xx), Rich header presence, section alignment. Return {linker, version?, evidence[]} per member; fixtures from gcc -fuse-ld=bfd/gold/lld (clang-18 present; lld missing -> note), tcc.\"},\n {\"id\":\"libc-runtime-fingerprint-facts\",\"concept\":\"Runtime / C library attribution: glibc vs musl vs uClibc vs bionic vs dietlibc, static vs dynamic vs static-pie, crt objects, bundled language runtimes\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"D27 builds were musl-DYNAMIC (PT_INTERP `/lib/ld-musl-x86_64.so.1`, NEEDED `libc.musl-x86_64.so.1`, musl src path `/home/buildozer/aports/main/musl/src/1.2.4` = Alpine) with Boehm GC + V builtin runtime bundled. Expose libc (glibc|musl|uclibc|bionic|dietlibc|none), libc_version (GLIBC_2.NN max verneed; musl from path strings), interpreter path, static/static-pie/dynamic, crt FILE symbols (crt1.c, crti, crtstuff.c), bundled runtimes (Boehm `GC_*`, `libgo`, Rust std, GHC rts). Answers verbatim from bytes; label set unknown -> keep lowercase library names.\"},\n {\"id\":\"stabs-debug-info-parser\",\"concept\":\"Parse STABS debug info (`.stab`/`.stabstr`, tcc -g, old gcc -gstabs, some Plan9/old toolchains): source files, functions, line table\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"D27 tcc build carried `.stab`/`.stabstr` instead of DWARF. Implement lib.binary.stabs(data) over the 12-byte nlist entries (u32 n_strx, u8 n_type, u8 n_other, u16 n_desc, u32 n_value): N_SO 0x64 (source/comp dir), N_SOL 0x84, N_FUN 0x24 (function name:type + address), N_SLINE 0x44 (line -> offset), N_GSYM/N_STSYM; return source_files, functions with addresses, debug_format='stabs'. Cross-check with `objdump -G F`. Lets a 'source file'/'function list'/'debug format' id be answered on a tcc member exactly as DWARF answers it on the gcc member.\"},\n {\"id\":\"cross-compiler-function-matching\",\"concept\":\"Match the SAME source function across different compilers' builds (gcc -Os+LTO vs tcc -O0: different code bytes, inlining, symbol survival)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"D27 twins share source but not codegen: the gcc LTO build kept ~200 symbols (main__main inlined/renamed with .lto_priv/.constprop), the tcc build ~1900. Byte-level diffing (stripped-twin-function-matching) fails here. Match by referenced string literals and constants, callee sets, CFG shape (block/edge counts), and symbol names after stripping IPA suffixes; output pairs {gcc_fn, tcc_fn, score, evidence}. Use capstone + pyelftools; angr CFGFast as fallback. Fixture: one C file built by gcc -O2 -flto and tcc.\"},\n {\"id\":\"pe-rich-header-toolchain-attribution\",\"concept\":\"PE toolchain attribution: Rich header (DanS, XOR key, comp.id = product id + build number -> MSVC version), linker version, MinGW vs MSVC vs clang-cl vs Borland/Delphi vs Go/Rust PE\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"Attribution sequel on the PE side (d02/d04/d10 already re-roll ELF<->PE). Decode Rich: find 'Rich' + key, xor back to 'DanS', list (prodid, build, count) and map prodid ranges to VS versions (VS2015-2022 = 14.x); no Rich -> not MSVC link.exe (MinGW/GNU ld, lld, Go, Delphi). Plus OptionalHeader Major/MinorLinkerVersion, `.CRT`/`.tls`/`.idata` (MinGW), `.text$mn` COMDAT (MSVC objects), RSDS PDB path, TimeDateStamp (reproducible builds = hash). pefile exposes RICH_HEADER; return {compiler, linker, vs_version?, evidence[]}.\"},\n {\"id\":\"compiler-flag-inference-facts\",\"concept\":\"Infer build flags / optimisation level when no producer string exists: -O0 vs -O2/-Os, frame pointers, -fstack-protector, _FORTIFY_SOURCE, CET/IBT, PIE, LTO, -ffunction-sections, -g level\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"D27 gcc producer listed `-Os -std=c99 -ffreestanding -fno-stack-protector -ffunction-sections -fdata-sections`; a stripped sequel would need inference: `push rbp; mov rbp,rsp` everywhere (-O0/-fno-omit-frame-pointer), `endbr64` (-fcf-protection), `__stack_chk_fail` refs, `__*_chk` imports (FORTIFY), ET_DYN+INTERP (PIE), `.lto_priv` suffixes (LTO), `.text.<fn>` input names (-ffunction-sections, visible only with tcc-style non-merging linkers). Return facts dict + evidence; spelling for checksec-style booleans true/false.\"},\n {\"id\":\"vlang-member-facts\",\"concept\":\"V-language identity facts for a d27 backfill: V module/function names (`<mod>__<fn>`), `_vinit`/`_vcleanup`, `_const_<mod>__<name>` constants, builtin runtime, GC presence, panic strings\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"Backfill candidates on the d27 group (the tcc build keeps all symbols; the gcc LTO build hides most): has_v_runtime (main__main/_vinit/builtin__), main function name, user-module function list (filter builtin__/strconv__/os__/GC_*/Array_*), constant symbols, Boehm GC version strings, `V panic: ` handler. Same field answered from each role member must tolerate missing symbols on the LTO build (fall back to strings).\"},\n {\"id\":\"transpile-to-c-language-identity\",\"concept\":\"Identify the SOURCE language beneath a C compiler for transpile-to-C languages: V (D27), Nim (D9), Vala/Genie (GObject), Cython, hxcpp (Haxe), Chicken Scheme, Eiffel, Mercury, ATS\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"Next new-language candidates in the D27 family. Cues: Vala `g_type_register_static`, `_vala_` helpers, GObject/GLib NEEDED; Cython `__pyx_` + `PyInit_`; hxcpp `hx::`/`__hxcpp_`; Chicken `C_toplevel`, `libchicken`; Nim `NimMain`; V `main__main`. Add each to the language detector with the compiler kept as a separate fact; HCFG stays raw/base64 in .rodata or an appended tail.\"},\n {\"id\":\"fuzzy-hash-family-attribution\",\"concept\":\"Family / build attribution by similarity: ssdeep, TLSH, imphash, telfhash, per-function normalized hashes; 'which member matches the reference', nearest neighbour across a group\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"'Attribute this binary to its maker' could continue as family attribution (D28-D30). Implement pure-Python TLSH/ssdeep if libs are missing (or pip ppdeep/py-tlsh into .venv), pefile imphash, telfhash (ELF import symbol TLSH), and a per-function mnemonic-sequence hash (capstone) with Jaccard similarity between members. Output lowercase hex digests exactly as the reference tools print them (ssdeep 'blocksize:hash1:hash2', TLSH 'T1' + 70 hex).\"},\n]\nfor g in new:\n    assert g['id'] not in byid, g['id']\ngaps=new+gaps\nfor g in gaps: assert set(g)=={'id','concept','priority','action','detail'}, g['id']\n# stable sort by priority so P1 first\ngaps=sorted(gaps,key=lambda g:g['priority'])\nout=\"\\n[\\n\"+\",\\n\".join(\"  \"+json.dumps(g,ensure_ascii=False) for g in gaps)+\"\\n]\\n\"\njson.loads(out)\nrest=rest[:i]+out+rest[j:]\nopen(p,'w').write(head+'## Readiness gaps'+rest)\nprint(len(gaps))\nEOF\npython3 -I $TMPDIR/gaps_edit.py","description":"Rewrite readiness gaps JSON with new gaps and re-ranking"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1048,"cache_read_input_tokens":144016,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1048},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b17b27cc-347b-41e9-a1e7-6aa9a3b67bd6","uuid":"76b64514-5bde-484c-ab6f-8d99e538ee26","timestamp":"2026-10-27T13:13:51.422Z","request_id":"req_011CgSoMvhBK8NunS42iNkFP","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_014vs3ubzV6V3iBm8RA62VCw":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; cat > $TMPDIR/gaps_edit.py <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\np='reference/coverage/binary-reverse-engineering.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nhead,rest=s.split('## Readiness gaps',1)\ni=rest.index('```json')+len('```json')\nj=rest.index('```',i)\nbody=rest[i:j]\ngaps=json.loads(body)\norig_lines=[l for l in body.strip().splitlines() if l.strip() not in ('[',']')]\nbyid={g['id']:g for g in gaps}\nassert len(byid)==len(gaps)\ndef setp(i,pr): byid[i]['priority']=pr\nfor i in ['crash-sidecar-generic-parser','jvm-call-chain-throw-site-facts','elf-core-dump-triage','faulting-instruction-locator',\n          'bug-reachability-gating-facts','crash-exploitability-facts','symbolic-input-solver','static-predicate-branch-evaluator']:\n    setp(i,2)\nsetp('diec',1)\nbyid['diec']['detail']+=\" D27 (compiler attribution: gcc vs tcc builds of one V source, no .comment) makes this the first-choice cross-check: DIE's compiler/linker signatures name tcc, gcc, clang, M