cept\":\"Match the SAME source function across different compilers' builds (gcc -Os+LTO vs tcc -O0: different code bytes, inlining, symbol survival)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"D27 twins share source but not codegen: the gcc LTO build kept ~200 symbols (main__main inlined/renamed with .lto_priv/.constprop), the tcc build ~1900. Byte-level diffing (stripped-twin-function-matching) fails here. Match by referenced string literals and constants, callee sets, CFG shape (block/edge counts), and symbol names after stripping IPA suffixes; output pairs {gcc_fn, tcc_fn, score, evidence}. Use capstone + pyelftools; angr CFGFast as fallback. Fixture: one C file built by gcc -O2 -flto and tcc.\"},\n {\"id\":\"pe-rich-header-toolchain-attribution\",\"concept\":\"PE toolchain attribution: Rich header (DanS, XOR key, comp.id = product id + build number -> MSVC version), linker version, MinGW vs MSVC vs clang-cl vs Borland/Delphi vs Go/Rust PE\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"Attribution sequel on the PE side (d02/d04/d10 already re-roll ELF<->PE). Decode Rich: find 'Rich' + key, xor back to 'DanS', list (prodid, build, count) and map prodid ranges to VS versions (VS2015-2022 = 14.x); no Rich -> not MSVC link.exe (MinGW/GNU ld, lld, Go, Delphi). Plus OptionalHeader Major/MinorLinkerVersion, `.CRT`/`.tls`/`.idata` (MinGW), `.text$mn` COMDAT (MSVC objects), RSDS PDB path, TimeDateStamp (reproducible builds = hash). pefile exposes RICH_HEADER; return {compiler, linker, vs_version?, evidence[]}.\"},\n {\"id\":\"compiler-flag-inference-facts\",\"concept\":\"Infer build flags / optimisation level when no producer string exists: -O0 vs -O2/-Os, frame pointers, -fstack-protector, _FORTIFY_SOURCE, CET/IBT, PIE, LTO, -ffunction-sections, -g level\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"D27 gcc producer listed `-Os -std=c99 -ffreestanding -fno-stack-protector -ffunction-sections -fdata-sections`; a stripped sequel would need inference: `push rbp; mov rbp,rsp` everywhere (-O0/-fno-omit-frame-pointer), `endbr64` (-fcf-protection), `__stack_chk_fail` refs, `__*_chk` imports (FORTIFY), ET_DYN+INTERP (PIE), `.lto_priv` suffixes (LTO), `.text.<fn>` input names (-ffunction-sections, visible only with tcc-style non-merging linkers). Return facts dict + evidence; spelling for checksec-style booleans true/false.\"},\n {\"id\":\"vlang-member-facts\",\"concept\":\"V-language identity facts for a d27 backfill: V module/function names (`<mod>__<fn>`), `_vinit`/`_vcleanup`, `_const_<mod>__<name>` constants, builtin runtime, GC presence, panic strings\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"Backfill candidates on the d27 group (the tcc build keeps all symbols; the gcc LTO build hides most): has_v_runtime (main__main/_vinit/builtin__), main function name, user-module function list (filter builtin__/strconv__/os__/GC_*/Array_*), constant symbols, Boehm GC version strings, `V panic: ` handler. Same field answered from each role member must tolerate missing symbols on the LTO build (fall back to strings).\"},\n {\"id\":\"transpile-to-c-language-identity\",\"concept\":\"Identify the SOURCE language beneath a C compiler for transpile-to-C languages: V (D27), Nim (D9), Vala/Genie (GObject), Cython, hxcpp (Haxe), Chicken Scheme, Eiffel, Mercury, ATS\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"Next new-language candidates in the D27 family. Cues: Vala `g_type_register_static`, `_vala_` helpers, GObject/GLib NEEDED; Cython `__pyx_` + `PyInit_`; hxcpp `hx::`/`__hxcpp_`; Chicken `C_toplevel`, `libchicken`; Nim `NimMain`; V `main__main`. Add each to the language detector with the compiler kept as a separate fact; HCFG stays raw/base64 in .rodata or an appended tail.\"},\n {\"id\":\"fuzzy-hash-family-attribution\",\"concept\":\"Family / build attribution by similarity: ssdeep, TLSH, imphash, telfhash, per-function normalized hashes; 'which member matches the reference', nearest neighbour across a group\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"'Attribute this binary to its maker' could continue as family attribution (D28-D30). Implement pure-Python TLSH/ssdeep if libs are missing (or pip ppdeep/py-tlsh into .venv), pefile imphash, telfhash (ELF import symbol TLSH), and a per-function mnemonic-sequence hash (capstone) with Jaccard similarity between members. Output lowercase hex digests exactly as the reference tools print them (ssdeep 'blocksize:hash1:hash2', TLSH 'T1' + 70 hex).\"},\n]\nfor g in new:\n    assert g['id'] not in byid, g['id']\ngaps=new+gaps\nfor g in gaps: assert set(g)=={'id','concept','priority','action','detail'}, g['id']\n# stable sort by priority so P1 first\ngaps=sorted(gaps,key=lambda g:g['priority'])\nout=\"\\n[\\n\"+\",\\n\".join(\"  \"+json.dumps(g,ensure_ascii=False) for g in gaps)+\"\\n]\\n\"\njson.loads(out)\nrest=rest[:i]+out+rest[j:]\nopen(p,'w').write(head+'## Readiness gaps'+rest)\nprint(len(gaps))\nEOF\npython3 -I $TMPDIR/gaps_edit.py","description":"Rewrite readiness gaps JSON with new gaps and re-ranking"}}}
